<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>DW - English for Africa</title><subtitle type="html">News, Analysis and Service from Germany and Europe - in 30 Languages</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa</id><updated>2026-11-17T17:43:07Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-africa" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-12756?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Fresh clashes at the Eritrean border — is Ethiopia sliding into a regional war?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4636e7b953aeeaf31d6f1a67266aef4aa25bb67fe0b4cff76642fbd63eee95d6</id><updated>2026-11-17T17:42:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T15:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fresh-clashes-at-the-eritrean-border-is-ethiopia-sliding-into-a-regional-war/a-79970353--d3d8ce7621b3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fresh-clashes-at-the-eritrean-border-is-ethiopia-sliding-into-a-regional-war/a-79970353?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Ethiopian troops push Tigrayan forces toward the Eritrean border, fears of a new regional war are growing. With tensions rising between Ethiopia, Eritrea and Sudan, the Horn of Africa faces uncertain times ahead.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Guinea jails 200 in wildcat gold mining crackdown</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3da7118f9c233a8f2e290f9f0bf70bd0da36c3148353ea703bb7d82970738551</id><updated>2026-11-17T17:43:07Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T12:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/guinea-jails-200-in-wildcat-gold-mining-crackdown/a-79968808--52f221020a34.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/guinea-jails-200-in-wildcat-gold-mining-crackdown/a-79968808?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Conakry court has jailed 22 former local officials from the gold-rich northeastern Siguiri region, as well as 200 people accused of illegal mining. It's part of a wider crackdown that sent thousands fleeing into Mali.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany joins 4 other EU states to set up Rwanda deportation hub</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9aa2ce5266d6575b97f4583f1da19dc4395b7e268d4c1535ee3aa58dd1baddea</id><updated>2026-11-17T17:41:55Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T12:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-joins-4-other-eu-states-to-set-up-rwanda-deportation-hub/a-79959158--227aa9c95b79.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-joins-4-other-eu-states-to-set-up-rwanda-deportation-hub/a-79959158?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The move follows approval of EU regulations that ease deportations and allow hubs to be set up outside the bloc. A similar scheme by the UK government fell apart over legal issues though the US has one up and running.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>South Africa: 17 killed in separate mass shooting incidents</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f183cd348ff7cf119efbc1e7e03c1e71bae00e4172ca357a5c4795ecd9c4274e</id><updated>2026-11-17T17:41:55Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T10:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-africa-17-killed-in-separate-mass-shooting-incidents/a-79956966--4668c90e6459.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-africa-17-killed-in-separate-mass-shooting-incidents/a-79956966?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Police are investigating two mass shooting incidents in Gauteng and KwaZulu-Natal provinces. There has been a growing trend of mass shooting incidents making headlines in recent years.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Nigeria's upcoming election marred by rising AI disinformation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:229044eb65f29fe020e51c060c2c09d06a6ce00955bf9d10d2d64b446e7d10e6</id><updated>2026-11-17T17:41:55Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T21:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nigeria-s-upcoming-election-marred-by-rising-ai-disinformation/a-79946897--e1618bd315dd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nigeria-s-upcoming-election-marred-by-rising-ai-disinformation/a-79946897?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Nigeria inches closer to the 2027 polls, the use of artificial intelligence in the electoral process has prompted questions about integrity and institutional readiness. Can Nigerians trust their democratic processes?</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
